      "id" : "note",
      "kind" : "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters" : {
        "text" : "# Seascape Shader\nThis workflow renders the user-supplied Seascape shader. The Seascape.metal Text node supplies the filename to Metal Render; keep the .metal file beside this workflow. Drag the Trackpad left or right to move the camera along the sea, and up or down to tilt its view. The first touch holds the camera at its current animation phase. The camera then stays fixed at the chosen position while the sea keeps moving. Reset the Trackpad to return to automatic camera motion. Four JSON Value nodes write the Trackpad coordinates, engaged flag, and first-touch Loop call into the JSON State pointer. This keeps the camera framing consistent between the card and full-size output. Loop advances shader time on each call. Change Width and Height to adjust output size. The source is attributed to Alexander Alekseev (TDM) and carries a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported notice in the .metal file."
      },
      "resources" : {

      },
      "title" : "How it works"
    },
